WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.110
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.390
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde Army,</i>

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.020
<i>who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.880
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.160
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.390
<i>Now, that's enough of 
the complicated stuff.</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.390
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:04.180
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.430
28 - Tachi
 <b>Uguisumaru</b>

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.760
<i>So it was Uguisumaru?</i>

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.740
I was trying to summon a nightingale, 
but instead you arrived, Hasebe.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.730
Just as I thought about catching 
a nightingale to show to Master,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.400
you're here, Uguisumaru.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.610
So are you going to take 
me to Master instead?

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.650
What a joke.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:00.690
That tree...

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.100
It has a nice look and feeling to it.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.740
What is it called?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.780
The tree's type?

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.900
It's a tree that even an old sword 
like me hasn't seen before,

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.910
which means...

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.830
What are they doing?

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.180
Found it!

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.240
It has four leaves!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.800
24 - Tantou
 <b>Hirano Toushirou</b>

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.310
Master told me all about this.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.510
White clovers usually have three leaves.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.480
But they said that the 
probability of one growing

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.770
with four leaves is one in ten thousand!

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:38.050
It's very valuable, so holding on to it 
means good things might happen.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:43.140
I wonder if I should give 
this to Uguisumaru-sama.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.810
Uguisumaru-sama?

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.210
What for?

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.780
I figured it might give me 
a chance to talk to him.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.330
Damn it!

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.240
What's the matter?

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.100
I dropped a dumbbell on my foot!

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.340
Are you all right?

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.700
When I went to take a 
bath, the water was cold.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:11.630
And when I went to put spices on 
my udon to eat it, the lid came off.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.970
I've had nothing but bad luck lately!

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.800
That is rather unfortunate.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:20.570
In that case, you should 
have this, Doudanuki-san.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.140
What is it?

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.720
It's a good luck charm.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.020
It doesn't look very 
nutritious. Is it any good?

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.340
Four-leaf clovers are incredibly rare.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.980
Good things might come your way.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.110
I gotcha.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.320
Take this.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.830
When I see those skinny arms 
of yours, I get concerned.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.470
No, it's fine—

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.710
We're supposed to be strong 
because we're weapons.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.080
Th-Thank you.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.340
Sure.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.710
Oh, Hirano.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.670
Perfect timing.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:31.970
Can you put that heavy thing you've 
got on top of the paper for me?

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.510
I-Is this okay?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.370
This is perfect.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.830
Now it won't get blown away.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:43.640
Isn't it better to close the sliding 
door if you're going to write?

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.820
You're unable to feel the seasons that way.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.760
You have to feel the breath of 
the earth to write properly.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.980
W-Wait, Tiger-kun!

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.160
You mustn't barge in!

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.180
<b>Flower Bud</b>

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.790
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.240
It's fine.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.930
Now, in return for the paperweight,

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.600
I will give you each a book from this shelf.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.570
Please take the tigers with you.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.970
Th-Thank you!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.270
Thank you!

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.210
<b>Mysteries of the Human Body</b>

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.160
<i>It looks really interesting,</i>

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.290
<i>but it might be a little difficult for me.</i>

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.440
It really is too much.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.470
What's that?

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:00.780
Yagen-niisan, it's a human body picture book.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:08.150
Transverse colon

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:08.150
Lungs

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.660
That's pretty neat.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.210
Where did you get this book?

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.300
Kasen-san gave it to me.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.970
That was very generous of him.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.030
Knowing more about the inside of 
the body leads to better medicine.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.940
Hey, would you mind giving me this book?

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.280
In exchange.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.100
What is this?

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:27.240
It's my latest creation.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.510
It'll lower fevers and stop coughing.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:32.240
But the flavor is a bit...

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.840
Incredibly suspicious, isn't it?

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.340
I'm sure it'll be useful, though.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.290
Hirano!

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.230
There's trouble that surprised even me!

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.270
It's Yamanbagiri!

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.030
Is he okay?

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:58.750
This is a surprising medicine that 
will cure anything if you take it.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:07:59.850
Thanks.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.610
Take it in one gulp, Yamanbagiri!

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:06.310
Yagen-niisan said he was still developing it,

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:07.970
so you probably shouldn't...

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:13.810
I'll be going.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.290
Far away!

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.200
Yamanbagiri!

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:17.430
Yamanbagiri!

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.730
Yamanbagiri-san!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:20.590
Yaman—

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.300
Don't call me pretty!

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.380
Yamanbagiri!

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.400
Are you better?

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.490
The death god at the Sanzu
River said that I was pretty.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.790
It's a good thing you didn't cross over.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.260
I'm sorry I worried you.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:33.090
It got rid of all the alcohol.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.410
Alcohol?

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.450
It seems he drank too much
 at yesterday's welcome party.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.110
Is that so?

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:40.600
As thanks.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.080
What beautiful fabric!

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:48.360
Kasen said that I needed a better
cloth and forced me to take it.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.900
But something like this doesn't suit me.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:52.830
Take it.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.260
Okay!

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:05.540
That looks warm.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.000
Are you bothered by the cold, Nikkari-san?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:12.020
That looks warm.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:14.690
<i>He said that twice.</i>

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:18.700
I know.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:21.450
I'll give you this instead.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:23.160
What is this thing?

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:28.240
At night, it softly envelops your 
whole exhausted body and mind.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.910
It's called a body pillow.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:30.880
Have you heard of it?

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:35.080
There's a gold ball as well, 
but I'm not giving that away.

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.790
Please call it gold armor.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.810
It's so warm...

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.850
27 - Tantou
 <b>Sayo Samonji</b>

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.740
That's...

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:49.180
It's called a "body pillow."

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:51.800
I've never used one before, though.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.360
Nii-sama.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.690
Do you want it?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.250
Nii-sama.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:01.640
Hirano-san, I'm sorry, but would you 
mind letting me have that body pillow?

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.610
Sure.

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.250
As thanks.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.960
I'll give you the key to my old playmate.

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.250
Old playmate?

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:19.680
Field duty.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.890
This is the kind of work you make 
an authentic Kotetsu do? Jeez.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.180
<b>Prestart    Off    On</b>

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.170
Um...

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.620
Does it go to this?

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:28.780
Wait just a minute.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.510
Hirano, what are you doing?

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.570
Ah, Hachisuka-san.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.020
Souza-san gave me this machine key.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.780
You won't be able to make it move.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.390
Won't you let me borrow that for a while?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.360
This is easy.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.470
It's the first time I've 
thought of field duty as fun!

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.720
Hirano, will you give this to me?

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:00.230
If it will be of use to you, Hachisuka-san.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:03.720
Castella Cake

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:03.620
I'll give you this in return.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:06.060
It's very delicious.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.100
Uguisumaru-sama.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.550
Hirano?

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:20.780
<b>Castella Cake</b>

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.770
Please have this Western 
treat with your tea.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.520
You're very thoughtful, Hirano.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:26.910
Western sweets, huh?

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.010
Let's have a look...

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.840
It's castella cake!

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:36.940
I've never had a fancy treat like that before.

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:39.160
Please have some, Mutsunokami-san.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.510
It's so good!

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:48.750
The taste reminds me of 
Western enlightenment.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:51.400
This is delicious!

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:52.210
All right!

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.860
I'll take a picture with this camera

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.650
of you saying "delicious" as 
you eat the castella cake.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.550
What are you doing?

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:04.380
Faces show up better when 
they're whitened, just hang on.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.030
Okay, now eat the castella cake!

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.900
It's delicious!

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:14.330
Now stop there! Smile!

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.030
Can we at least drink some tea?

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.010
That'll make it blurry!

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:20.850
Just stay very still.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.030
<i>At first I had a four-leaf clover.</i>

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:29.550
<i>But in the end, I got my picture taken,
 smiling with Uguisumaru-sama.</i>

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:33.000
<i>It was a good thing.</i>

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.660
Can we move yet, Mutsunokami?

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.980
You mustn't speak!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.990
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:00.540
I'm exhausted.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:01.810
Good job today.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:03.590
What are you doing?

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:04.710
That.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.850
I was just thinking about how it'd be nice

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.890
if I could show Ichi-nii how 
happy our brothers are.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:13.220
Ichi-nii?

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.660
Ichigo Hitofuri.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:16.520
Yagen and the others' older brother.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.920
Osayo seems to be having fun, too.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:22.230
I'm sure if Kousetsu-niisama could 
see this, he would be pleased.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:26.960
They don't really talk about 
their brother very much.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.180
Why's that?

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:30.200
They don't know when they'll see him.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:32.760
It's possible they might never get to.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:36.750
So they hold back that 
longing in their hearts.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.120
Do you have a minute?

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.850
What on earth is this tree?

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.540
Kashuu, you're the oldest 
member of this citadel, right?

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:52.980
Don't you have general 
understanding of this place?

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.230
I don't know.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:56.530
I've barely been here a year.

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:58.830
Uguisumaru asked me about it,

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:00.290
and it's been bothering me.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.770
I have no idea what kind of tree it is.

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.690
It's not a zelkova or a hackberry tree.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:07.790
And judging by the roots,
 it's not a cherry tree, either.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.980
What? It's not a cherry tree?

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.530
No, most likely not.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.410
It's not a cherry tree?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:15.880
Are you sure?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.290
26 - Tantou
 <b>Atsushi 
Toushirou</b>

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:17.460
So, it's not a cherry tree...

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.760
All of you want a cherry tree?

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:25.460
If it were a cherry tree, 
it should have buds by now.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:29.580
Well, as soon as its leaves come in, we'll 
be able to tell what kind of tree it is.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.450
I wish it was a cherry tree.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:34.670
A-A cherry tree would be nice.

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:35.900
That's right!

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.140
We'd like a cherry tree!

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.600
25 - Wakizashi
 <b>Honebami Toushirou</b>

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:38.570
Cherry tree.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.880
Isn't there a way to make 
it be a cherry tree somehow?

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:44.480
You too, Yamatonokami?

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.080
It's impossible, of course.

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:48.860
If we go back in time to 
when Hanasaka-jiisan lived,

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:51.080
couldn't we borrow some ash from him?

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:52.780
That's a good idea.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:57.890
It would be, if he were real,

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.600
but that's just a fairy tale.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:01.740
Well, we'll figure it out somehow.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:02.820
Like how?!

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:05.680
What if we hypnotize it?

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.730
You are a cherry tree.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.920
You are a cherry tree.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.530
You are a cherry tree.

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:16.590
I-I am a cherry tree!

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:18.550
What point is there in you
getting hypnotized instead?!

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:21.910
It looks like we only have this method left.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:22.820
Nii-sama?

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:31.820
I heard that dead bodies are buried 
beneath beautiful cherry trees.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.430
Maybe if we bury a dead 
body under this tree...

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:36.980
No, no, no, no!

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:39.110
Don't say something so disturbing!

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.610
Nii-sama.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:44.370
Well then, what if we make 
a wish on this tree directly?

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:46.800
What are you saying?

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.590
Does everyone have one?

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:52.970
What are we doing, here?

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:56.140
We'll write our wish, "I wish 
cherry blossoms would bloom,"

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:58.560
on these papers and hang
 them on the branches.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.290
And what's that going to do?

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:05.390
If we write a bunch of them and hang them 
on the tree, maybe the tree will listen.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:09.060
Come on, that's not a very realistic idea.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:12.300
That might be a good idea.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:16.470
I've heard that if you put your feelings in 
your writing, your wish will come true.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:17.320
Really?

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.530
I haven't heard that before.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:24.320
If we place our wishes directly 
on the tree, it just might work!

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:25.040
Surely.

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:27.550
We won't know unless we try, right?

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:30.260
D-Does that mean it will be like Tanabata?

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.520
I'm not sure.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:35.140
Okay, we'll write lots of them, 
tie them to the branches,

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.010
and make lots of wishes on the tree.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.260
Jeez.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:43.630
I'll go get the paper ready, then.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.350
We'll do a hundred papers per sword.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.470
A hundred?!

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:48.690
The more wishes the better, right?

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:54.150
I guess I'll write some, too.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.980
Okay, start!

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.990
"I wish cherry blossoms will bloom."

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.590
"I wish..."

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.790
"...cherry blossoms will bloom."

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.180
All right, I'm on my third!

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:10.870
I-I'm on my third one, too.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:13.810
Yamatonokami-san! More paper please!

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:14.380
Okay!

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:18.610
Cherry blossoms, cherry 
blossoms, cherry bloss...

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.810
Things have gotten pretty interesting.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.630
Isn't my cherry blossom drawing good?

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.780
What good is this going to do?

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:31.870
Here, you write a bunch, too, Hasebe-san!

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:33.710
Give it your best everyone!

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:34.860
Our goal is a thousand!

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.110
It increased?!

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:41.120
I wish cherry blossoms would bloom.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.590
I'm tired.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.890
My fingers are stiff.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:45.090
Ah, you're writing the wrong thing!

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:46.080
Don't look!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:21.190
I wish cherry blossoms would bloom.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.390
It's at full bloom.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:46.430
Pretty.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.070
It is indeed.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:51.140
So that's it.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:54.550
You used pink paper on the back.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.800
<b>bloom</b>

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.520
<b>Please bloom</b>

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:34.120
They did a good job.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:41.990
<b>I want to see Ichi-nii</b>

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.660
<b>I want to play with Ichi-nii</b>

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.660
<b>I want to see Kousetsu-niisama</b>

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.120
<b>I hope Ichi-nii
 gets here soon</b>

00:19:55.670 --> 00:20:00.090
I've heard that if you put your feelings in 
your writing, your wish will come true.

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:00.790
Really?

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:12.900
There're so many wishes.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:16.530
Everyone.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.400
Is that a bud?

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:29.790
Th-Th-They're cherry blossoms!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:30.660
Cherry blossoms?

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:36.970
Cherry blossom buds?!

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:39.590
H-Here, too!

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:42.280
There weren't any just a minute ago.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:44.850
Our wish came true, didn't it?

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:48.870
Did it truly listen to our wishes?

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:53.120
I-I-I have to let Master know!

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:56.390
Master!

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.390
Someone once said,

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.530
"If you see a tree you've never seen before,

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.950
it might be a ten thousand leaf cherry tree."

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:11.860
Ten thousand leaf cherry tree?

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:15.460
A miraculous cherry tree that blooms 
only once every ten thousand years.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:20.150
It will grant the wishes 
of anyone who sees it.

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:25.160
Ten thousand, huh?

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:57.670
I want to play 
with Ichi-nii

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:06.430
<i>If this really is a miraculous 
tree that can grant wishes,</i>

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:09.380
<i>I hope it will grant everyone's wishes.</i>

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.040
<i>Including mine.</i>

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:21.360
<b>I will protect Okita-kun</b>

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.390
<i>Until then, I'll have to get stronger.</i>

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
